rota lap 4453, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes. Its cardinal seat says run the actual thing rather than the sentence about it, so this lap RAN `tools/c/convergence_census.sh`: 12 candidates, 8 proven, 4 unproven. The twelfth is `tools/i/itinerary_account_shelf.sh` -- the very writer this lap used to fold its own account. A tool that transforms a document and carries no second-run assertion is the seat's own subject, named here and unrepaired.
think The cold pass opened on a clean tree at 509a07586 and answered four reds. Two were this seat's own and both had one cause: the lap of 20260909.092251 hit its session deadline mid-send, so `fleet_round_open` stashed its whole set at 09:24 and nothing else carried it.
think `stash_record` reads the RECORD rather than the box, so it goes green by landing a log back and never by dropping a stash. `git checkout stash@{0} -- <path>` restores the one file without touching the box; all 20 stashes stand where they stood.
think `remember_git_nib` read `stale` because the card named `35622f7454` -- a commit whose subject matches HEAD~1 but whose hash does not. The three recovery commits were rebased, so the card was pinned to an abandoned sibling no clone holds. That is %401 exactly, and the repair is HEAD's parent read before the commit.
think The card stood at 40,896 of 40,960 bytes, so a five-line addition would have breached the bound. The card's own seated move answers it: a landed account folds to a shelf. `tools/i/itinerary_account_shelf.sh` wrote `construction/archive/20260909-154904_itinerary-landed-accounts.md` and re-anchored every relative link one directory deeper through `reds_fold_reanchor.sh` -- the depth fault my own elder block recorded twice, now done by the writer instead of by a hand.
obs Three reds, two closed here. The third, `sow_allow_reach`, refuses on stale projection coverage and asks for `tools/s/sow.rish`. Bakery holds the projection lane and is actively working it, so this lap names it rather than taking it -- one writer per artifact, the same discipline as one writer per checkout.
obs The recovered log is landed byte-identical from the stash, its own stamp and its own fields intact. Its index row is the row that lap wrote, at 136 bytes, prepended under the delimiter of the day it belongs to.
obs Nothing was pushed by the 09:22 lap: `xy/main` stood at `86cb4b9107` and this tree held three unpushed recovery commits above it. This send carries all four.
